Spec: Feature raw_ingestion index for per-correlation_id lookups

Purpose:
  Speed up the transformation job, which needs ~5 minutes for 500 records in PROD (`raw_ingestion` with ~82k rows).
  The claim query (HAVING subquery and UPDATE) and `load_counterparts` look up fragments per `(topic, correlation_id)` including status `processed`.
  `idx_raw_pending_topics` only covers status `pending`, so each aggregate caused sequential scans over the whole table.

Platform: PostgreSQL

References:
  ../../../mitm-2.sdd
  ../../../transformation-layer/transformation-layer.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /transformation-layer/migrations/**
  /migrations/setup.sql
  /docs/Transformation-layer/README.md
  /CHANGELOG.md

Decisions:
  Column order `(topic, correlation_id, status, source_system, created_at DESC)`: `topic` and `correlation_id` are equality filters in all three queries, `status` serves `IN ('pending','processed')`, `source_system, created_at DESC` serve `COUNT(DISTINCT source_system)` and the `DISTINCT ON` ordering of `load_counterparts`.
  Partial index `WHERE correlation_id IS NOT NULL`, because the job ignores fragments without `correlation_id`.
  Plain `CREATE INDEX` instead of `CONCURRENTLY`: at ~82k rows the build takes seconds, and the statement also works when `setup.sql` runs inside a transaction.
  The index belongs to the transformation migrations (not `collector-layer`), because only the transformation job needs it.

Must:
  `idx_raw_topic_correlation` exists on `raw_ingestion`.
  The migration is idempotent (safe to re-run with `setup.sql`).

Must not:
  Change code in `mitm_transformation_main` or the collector layer.
  Change or drop `idx_raw_pending_topics`.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Add `transformation-layer/migrations/010_raw_ingestion_correlation_index.sql`.
  [x] #2 Append the migration to `migrations/setup.sql`.
  [x] #3 Update `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/Transformation-layer/README.md`.
  [ ] #4 Verify on the dev database: run the migration, re-run it, check the plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)`.
  [ ] #5 Run in PROD and compare the run time for 500 records.

Done when:
  `\d raw_ingestion` lists `idx_raw_topic_correlation`, re-running the migration changes nothing, and the plans of the claim query and `load_counterparts` use the index instead of `Seq Scan on raw_ingestion`.

Scenario: migration re-run
  Given `idx_raw_topic_correlation` already exists
  When the migration runs again
  Then nothing changes

Scenario: counterpart lookup
  Given `raw_ingestion` contains processed fragments of many correlation_ids
  When the transformation job loads the counterparts of one aggregate
  Then the plan uses `idx_raw_topic_correlation`
